Looking at the outline, the red dots at (245,103), (758,51), (930,361), (788,621), (357,668), and (72,565) are the true corners where the direction changes sharply. The other six dots—(505,76), (845,211), (865,481), (585,641), (196,610), (152,341)—lie straight along the edges between those corners, so they don't create new sides.

Thus the closed outline is a hexagon: top edge, upper-right edge, lower-right edge, bottom edge, lower-left edge, and upper-left edge.

